WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.125 --> 00:00:15.291
When will Lord Sarver and your master of basketball operations be arriving?

00:00:15.291 --> 00:00:18.125
They have entrusted me as emissary. Now what is this trade?

00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:19.583
Trade? No

00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:22.666
We’ve come to discuss an alliance

00:00:22.666 --> 00:00:24.166
An alliance?

00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:25.625
How would that even work?

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.375
Think of it more as a merger

00:00:27.375 --> 00:00:29.416
Individually, our houses are weak

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.875
but together, we can dominate the West as House Kings Suns!

00:00:35.916 --> 00:00:38.500
[Triumphant Horn]

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.375
Eh...don’t love it

00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:45.625
But hold on. But what if I told you you
could play alongside the next Steph Curry?

00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:46.583
[Laughter]

00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:51.250
Right. It’s just the name “Kings Suns.” It’s awkward

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.166
What about Sun Kings?

00:00:53.166 --> 00:00:55.708
OK fine, from here on we are House Sun Kings, OK?

00:00:55.708 --> 00:00:56.375
We are the Sun Kings

00:00:56.375 --> 00:00:58.166
We are the Sun Kings
[Triumphant Horn]

00:00:58.541 --> 00:01:02.583
We’ve taken the liberty of drafting a standard for our new combined house

00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:03.583
Buddy!

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.041
Flip it one more

00:01:09.125 --> 00:01:10.541
I can’t really see the sun

00:01:10.541 --> 00:01:12.416
What do y--It’s in the front of the crown!

00:01:12.416 --> 00:01:13.500
Uh, excuse me

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.833
I was thinking maybe…I was thinking maybe a crown inside a sun?

00:01:17.833 --> 00:01:19.875
Ooh like a fiery crown. I like that.

00:01:19.875 --> 00:01:23.250
Thanks yeah, I like to paint so…I think about like compositions and stuff

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.291
I think it’s great. We want that. The flaming crown

00:01:25.291 --> 00:01:29.375
Oh come on! Buddy and Bogdan spent like three practices stitching this together!

00:01:29.375 --> 00:01:31.166
It’s fine, it’s fine, my lord. 

00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:34.291
It is a small price to pay for a dragon

00:01:34.291 --> 00:01:35.416
Dragon?

00:01:35.416 --> 00:01:38.166
Yes.  Everyone is actually quite keen to have a look

00:01:38.166 --> 00:01:39.375
You mean Dragan?

00:01:39.375 --> 00:01:39.708
Huh?

00:01:39.916 --> 00:01:41.000
I mean, here he is

00:01:41.625 --> 00:01:42.833
That’s a bit of a shit dragon

00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:43.541
Where’s its wings?

00:01:43.541 --> 00:01:44.625
And scales?!

00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:46.250
I’m still developing you guys, come on

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:49.208
Oh I see, so the dragon is actually a person

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:52.000
Great job researching, Vlade, really good researching there

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.041
I didn’t realize–I just read the notes the scouts gave me, they said dragon

00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:57.791
Did you draft De'Aaron Fox because you thought he was a fox?

00:01:58.291 --> 00:01:59.583
Foxes are smart

00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:02.041
Ugh God. It’s fine, it’s fine

00:02:02.041 --> 00:02:06.625
We can evaluate all our assets when we join forces in Sacramento!

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:07.916
You mean in Phoenicia

00:02:07.916 --> 00:02:10.750
Oh for heaven sakes! We just built a state-of-the-art castle

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.666
Isn’t Sacramento a bit small?

00:02:12.666 --> 00:02:15.666
You want us to go to Phoenicia when It’s a hundred
and f--king twenty degrees every day?!

00:02:15.666 --> 00:02:17.041
It gets cool at night

00:02:17.041 --> 00:02:21.291
And besides, do you expect us to abandon a city with such a rich basketball history?

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:25.666
Well clearly you are not familiar with the rich history of House Kings

00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:27.916
Lord Commander Adelman and his

00:02:27.916 --> 00:02:28.458
Lord Commander Adelman and his
Adelman

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.416
...corner offense?

00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:33.083
Oh come on, they don’t even compare to D’Antoni’s Seven Seconds or Less offense!

00:02:33.083 --> 00:02:34.875
What are you talking? We had Chris Webber!

00:02:34.875 --> 00:02:35.750
Ser Charles was better

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:40.583
That’s ridiculous, man, Webber was bigger, he was more athletic, not even close, man

00:02:40.583 --> 00:02:42.750
And you had nothing like Peja Stojakovic

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:43.958
He was no Dan Majerle

00:02:43.958 --> 00:02:46.208
All right this guy doesn’t know what he’s talking about with Dan Majerle

00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:47.791
Dan Majerle was trash, man

00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:50.333
And I suppose you’re going to say the same of Steve Nash!

00:02:50.666 --> 00:02:53.375
The Kings have never come close to talent like that

00:02:53.375 --> 00:02:54.958
What about the White Knight of Chocolate?

00:02:54.958 --> 00:02:59.541
Wait, wait, wait. Did you just compare Jason Williams to Steve Nash?

00:02:59.541 --> 00:03:00.625
Have you gone mental?

00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:02.583
Well Steve Nash never did an elbow pass

00:03:02.625 --> 00:03:03.666
Who gives a shit?

00:03:03.666 --> 00:03:05.208
What do you know about passing, ball hog?

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.583
All right, enough, enough!

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.083
Maybe we are a bunch of ball hogs

00:03:09.208 --> 00:03:11.416
And maybe it is bloody hot in Phoenicia

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.291
And sure Sacramento’s...

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.166
smaller than Tucson. I don’t even know where it is to be honest

00:03:16.666 --> 00:03:18.916
But if we put aside our differences, 

00:03:19.458 --> 00:03:21.291
and combine our houses

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:22.291
well then

00:03:22.875 --> 00:03:25.208
we still probably wouldn’t make the playoffs but

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:26.583
Oh boy

00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:29.083
Wh-When I look around, 

00:03:29.416 --> 00:03:31.833
I see a bunch of guys who,

00:03:32.375 --> 00:03:34.333
I may not know their names, and 

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:37.291
they may not be good, but they play

00:03:37.708 --> 00:03:39.166
Basketball I think

00:03:39.916 --> 00:03:40.583
And...

00:03:40.583 --> 00:03:42.125
Eric…make your point

00:03:42.416 --> 00:03:43.791
I guess my point is…

00:03:44.541 --> 00:03:46.583
Eh…I don’t know, I don’t even wanna be here

